// Title: Potential DLL Sideloading Using Coregen.exe
// Sigma ID: 0fa66f66-e3f6-4a9c-93f8-4f2610b00171
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-12-31 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, stealth, T1218, T1055
// Description: Detect usage of the "coregen.exe" (Microsoft CoreCLR Native Image Generator) binary to sideload
//   arbitrary DLLs.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/OtherMSBinaries/Coregen/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/image_load/image_load_side_load_coregen.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceImageLoadEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\coregen.exe" and (not((FolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Microsoft Silverlight\\" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft Silverlight\\" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\System32\\" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\SysWOW64\\")))
